course: dictionary
lesson: 14134
title: Minimise: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «minimise» is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. The clues are the words next to it.
explain: To minimise something means to make it as small or as little as possible. «We wear helmets to minimise the risk of injury.» The word risk is the clue: we make the danger smaller. Try swapping in "make smaller" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also mean to make something seem less important than it really is. «Do not minimise her worries; she is really scared.» The words really scared show the worries are serious, so minimise here means to act as if they matter less, which is the wrong thing to do.
fact: Minimise means to make something as small or as little as possible.
fact: «Minimise» can also mean to make something seem less important or serious than it is.
fact: On a computer, to minimise a window shrinks it to a small button or icon.
fact: In maths and science, minimise can mean finding the smallest value, such as the least waste.
fact: In American English the word is spelled minimize, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: «We wear helmets to minimise the risk of injury.» What does minimise mean here? | Ignore the rules completely | Paint the helmet a bright colour | *Make the risk as small as possible | Make the risk as big as possible
exercise: «Please do not minimise how upset he is.» What does minimise mean here? | Write his feelings down in a list | *Make his feelings seem less serious than they are | Measure how tall he is | Make his feelings louder
exercise: «Tap the button to minimise the window.» What happens to the window? | It closes and cannot be opened again | *It shrinks to a small icon | It grows to fill the whole screen | It changes colour
test: Our science teacher asked us to minimise the waste from the experiment. What does she want? | Find the largest amount of waste | Ask for more waste | *Make the waste as small as possible | Put the waste in the sink
test: Sam wanted to minimise the window so he could see his homework. What did Sam do? | *Shrank the window to a small icon | Made the window bigger | Changed the screen to green | Closed his homework for ever
exam: Which sentence uses minimise to mean make something seem less important? | «The shop opens at nine.» | «We will minimise the waste from our lunch.» | «Please minimise the window now.» | *«Don't minimise the problem; it is very serious.»
